{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791125551,"nonce":"xXSn7e7P8E53uQX1TtZ8uQhELFI=","message":"TypeMeta onto TypeDesc (M2): f17d26d (zyntax 174f11f7b42eeb995d968ad365a0693a1e237a58, zyntax git-bug 5daa6e7, by zyntax-07; not on origin yet, so f17d26d waits to push). Every reference type's objects start with a header word filled from a per-type global the runtime fills through HostHeap v2's type_header slot. Caribou's type_header (caribou_zyntax::object) makes a core TypeDesc per type and layout: fields from HostTypeInfo, methods from the published class; the language is the one caribou marks as compiling around compile_module/reload_typed_program. Each published class records its descriptors, so an outgoing object's word 0 is compared, never dereferenced; a match crosses as the object itself, otherwise as the proxy. Python class instances now cross direct (tests/python_objects.rs asserts it; also under ASH_GC_STRESS=50). Publish now recognises the header field (object_header::header_field) when matching the HIR struct to a class. Remaining in this issue: zrtl and caribou_abi, for which a performance-first spec is with zyntax-07 (measured today: a Python call to a plugin costs 120 ns on the float path and 306 ns on the boxed path, against a few ns for a direct call).","files":null}]}